# Alerts

An alert is born in a hook, goes through `addAlert`/`addAlerts` in the store
(which dedups), and renders in `AlertBar` (timeline) and the per-symbol ribbon.

## The ten types

`price` `filing` `news` `catalyst` `trade_exchange` `scanner` `tweet`
`tradingview` `rss` `mail` — the union on `Alert.type` in `types/index.ts`.
Adding one means touching the type, `lib/alertTypeColor.ts`, the subscription
UI, and the audio defaults. Miss one and the alert fires with no color, no
sound, or no way to subscribe.

## Every alert needs a dedupKey

Same alert arrives by several routes — SignalR live, REST poll, and the
60-second auditor backfill. `dedupKey` is what stops three copies. Follow the
existing `source:id` convention:

    pr:{storyId}          fpr:{storyId}        tx:{postId}
    filing:{cik}-{dcn}    tweet:{id}:{symbol}  tv:{alertId}
    cat:{symbol}-{iso}    at:{guid}            gain:{symbol}:{date}

Prefer a stable server-side id. Never use `Date.now()` in a dedupKey — it
defeats the entire mechanism, because the same alert arriving twice gets two
different keys.

## Colors are inline hex, never Tailwind classes

`lib/alertTypeColor.ts` returns hex strings applied via `style={{ color }}`.
This is not a style preference. Tailwind's content scan covers `app/` and
`components/` only — **class names written in `lib/` are purged from the CSS
bundle**. That's a real bug that shipped: every alert type lost its color
except filings. Use inline hex anywhere outside `app/`/`components/`.

## Filtering

- `lib/excludePrPatterns.ts` — ambulance-chaser / class-action PR blacklist.
  Applies to headline types only, never to price or scanner alerts
- `lib/filteredPr.ts` — the user's own keyword rules:
  comma = OR, `&` = AND, `!` = NOT, `*` = wildcard. Ported from the legacy
  C# app; keep the semantics identical
- `config.excludeFilings` — pipe-separated SEC form types

## Reducing alert count is a bug until proven otherwise

If a change makes fewer alerts appear, that is the failure mode of this app,
not a successful filter. Say so explicitly in the diff and explain why the
dropped ones should be dropped.
